1.0.0 (unreleased)
------------------------
Viewer-only restructure of the repository:
- Removed the editor Flask backend, CDN staging and all legacy build artifacts
- Replaced webpack with Vite (dev/build/preview), default Vite project layout
- Converted the source to strict TypeScript (target ES2022, noImplicitAny, no explicit any)
- Replaced Leaflet with OpenLayers; IIIF Image API replaces Zoomify (breaking: map_type "zoomify" is gone, use "iiif")
- Converted Less to SASS with zero deprecation warnings (@use only, no @import, no vendor prefixes, no postcss-scss)
- Fonts bundled via @fontsource + @fontsource-utils/scss mixins (woff2, latin subsets); no runtime font CDN requests
- New exchange format: IIIF Presentation API 3.0 manifests (docs/storymap-as-iiif-manifest.md) with navPlace geo +
  a storymap: extension; all example fixtures converted and validated against the official IIIF validator;
  StoryMap reads both legacy JSON and Presentation 3 manifests
- JSON Schema for storymap data: runtime validation with console error reporting + CLI validator
- ESLint (all rules enabled, TS mixins per the handbook replace runtime classMixin), Stylelint (zero disabled
  rules), Prettier, GitHub Actions for CI (lint/typecheck/validate/tests/build/e2e) and release packaging
- Dropped code for pre-2022 browsers: XHR -> fetch, removed vendor detection, engine workarounds, pollers,
  minEmoji sprite polyfill and Knight Lab tracking
- Bug fixes: null-offset crashes, IIIF source races, unique-id generation, swipe direction check, empty-block cleanup
- Stacked raster overlays with per-layer presentation (opacity, visibility,
  attribution, className, blendMode, lon/lat extent), runtime setters and
  setMapOption rebuild; minimap overview constraint via overview_extent
- Slide transition events (transitionstart/transitionend), guaranteed goTo
  change events, opt-in global keyboard navigation
- Runtime language switching without reload (MenuBar.refreshLabels,
  StoryMap.refreshLanguage); locale fallback no longer mutates English;
  German fullscreen labels
- Attribution refresh on basemap switch (+setExtraAttributions); identical
  credits collapse to one entry; route lines pinned above rebuilt tile
  layers; font_css resolves page-relative; slide colors accept any CSS color

